(Introduction to Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Retrieval-Augmented Generation \(RAG\) is a technique that combines a retriever with a) Tj T*
(language model. Instead of relying only on knowledge stored in model weights, the system) Tj T*
(looks up relevant passages in an external knowledge base and gives them to the model as) Tj T*
(context. RAG was introduced by Lewis et al. in 2020.) Tj T*
(The main advantage of RAG is that knowledge can be updated without retraining. Adding a) Tj T*
(new document only requires embedding it and inserting it in the index.) Tj T*
ET
