(Introduction to Retrieval-Augmented Generation) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Vector embeddings map text to points in a high-dimensional space so that semantically) Tj T*
(similar passages are close together. Sentence-Transformers models such as all-MiniLM-L6-v2) Tj T*
(produce 384-dimensional embeddings. Similarity is usually measured with cosine similarity.) Tj T*
(Vector databases like ChromaDB, FAISS and Pinecone use approximate nearest neighbour) Tj T*
(search \(for example HNSW graphs\) to find the closest chunks in milliseconds, even with) Tj T*
(hundreds of thousands of vectors.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
